  "architecture": {
    "control": "Existing ANF :try and clauses; private signals bind Source error/throw/exit/raise to the actual machine frame. Non-Source failures mark the private abort bit and bypass handlers and Source cleanup.",
    "values": "Actual normalized exceptions receive private current-frame witnesses. CompilerData walks all their fields; external first-order input/result rules remain unchanged. Owned pure callables cannot escape a failed request.",
    "normalization": "Actual VM frames bounded to64 entries, arguments projected to arity, locations restricted to file/line. No formatter-hook metadata reaches Exception.normalize. No raw catch token is manufactured.",
    "lowering": "Canonical fn and case failure paths are explicit, so Core optimization cannot infer different failure classes.",
    "usage": "Source try/catch/finally; raw erlang throw/error/exit/raise; existing ExInfo raise_payload and fixed Core ex-info/ex-data/ex-original adapters. No evaluator callback or caller-selected primitive policy."
  },
